    "title": "D.D. Meighen Humanity in Action Award: The Rev. Dick Bowyer showcases selfless commitment to Fairmont | Fairmont News | wvnews.com",
    "text": "FAIRMONT, W.Va. — The Marion County Chamber of Commerce’s newest annual award is the D.D. Meighen Humanity in Action Award, and officials believe nobody in the community showcases Meighen’s selfless commitment to Fairmont and beyond more than the Rev. Richard Bowyer.\nA native of Huntington, Bowyer has earned degrees from Marshall University, Duke University, West Virginia University and Fairmont State University. He joined the West Virginia Conference of the United Methodist Church in 1960 and served as the campus minister at Fairmont State’s Wesley Foundation for 43 years until his retirement in 2005.",
    "summary": "FAIRMONT, W.Va. — The Marion County Chamber of Commerce’s newest annual award is the D.D. Meighen Humanity in Action Award, and officials believe nobody in the community showcases Meighen’s selfless commitment to Fairmont and beyond more than the Rev. Richard Bowyer. A native of Huntington, Bowyer has earned degrees from Marshall University, Duke University, West Virginia University and Fairmont State University. He joined the West Virginia Conference of the United Methodist Church in 1960 and served as the campus minister at Fairmont State’s Wesley Foundation for 43 years until his retirement in 2005.",
